  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "The centre of a circle is located at $(1,2)$. The circle passes through the point $(3,5)$. Find the equation of the tangent to the circle at this point. Write your answer in the form $ax+by=c$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$2x+3y=21$.",
      "worked": "The radius has gradient $m_r=\\frac{5-2}{3-1}=\\frac{3}{2}$. The tangent is perpendicular to the radius, hence $m_t=-\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-5&=-\\frac{2}{3}(x-3)\\\\3y-15&=-2(x-3)\\\\3y-15&=-2x+6\\\\2x+3y&=21.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 54
  },
